Z||000000||htiek||10-12-2001||10:30 AM||||Hey guys, hows it going.  I just registered on the forum, i dont know why it took so long, Ive been finding information on this site forever now and i have question for you fiero experts.<P>Right now i drive a 1984 4-cyl fiero, with an auto.  The other day i drove by a yard with a 1985 fiero gt for sale.  I would like to own a 6-cyl fiero, and its also a 4 speed, and ive been looking for a manual.<P>I just wanted to know if you guys thought that it would be worth it to purchase this fiero. <P>1985 Fiero Gt<BR>6-cyl 4-speed<BR>113000 miles<BR>for 1500-1800(have to settle on a price)<P>So whats up<BR>any response would be appreciated<P>||||reg||7
Z||000001||Voytek||10-12-2001||10:44 AM||||Where is Lowell?<P>Welcome.<P>Price sounds half decent if the car is in good shape.  Is it in good shape?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cozmo||10-12-2001||10:46 AM||||Welcome!<BR>Forumist... I love it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>The price seems high on the '85 GT you're looking at but a lot depends on the condition.<BR>If you've been reading the forum a while you're probably getting familiar with some of the quirks and foibles the Fiero has.  Look at all the known "problem areas", add up what needs to be fixed and explain to the seller what it will take for you to bring the car up to snuff.<BR>Luckily, Fieros are just beginning to appreciate in value so there are still some pretty good deals out there.<BR>Good luck, post some pics if you buy it...<BR>Again, welcome to the Forum!<P><P>------------------<BR><B>BobC</B><BR><B>'85 2M6 Targa</B><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/targsig.jpg"> <BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||10-12-2001||10:55 AM||||The 85 GT was a great coupe styled Fiero.  With a 16 year old car, depending on how the car was maintained, can be a good purchase for 15-1800 bucks. I know many Fieros are still running fantastically with twice the milage and many that are beat with half the milage.<P>Is it running? does the engine making any knocking noises, smoking, check condition of the oil.  Check for rust, pull back the side trunk carpet behind the wheel well.<P>Drive the car, the steering will be "stiff" when you go slow, but should be firm once you are moving.  Does it track straight, does it stop straight, does the E brake work. Take a T-11 driver, pull the panel off to get to the panel to read the, if any, error codes. Check the coolant color, condition or if oil is present.||||reg||1
Z||000004||htiek||10-12-2001||11:05 AM||||The only visible problem from a quick overlook, was that the guy began to sand the top of the car down.  He did the hood, to rear clip, the decklid, and the roof.  The car drives great, handles better than my 84, and has all factory options.  Im trying to talk the guy into some kind of deal.  Most of my argument is with the condition of the paint work.  <P>I wish he wasnt lazy and would finish the job, but i guess it gives me something to do in my spare time.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||htiek||10-12-2001||11:07 AM||||Lowell is in Massachusetts.||||reg||1
